s1-p23 = prose (cons "**Routines, relations, and rationales.** The reasoning establishing a relation is itself a construction. A rationale takes evidence as input and constructs evidence as output; a routine transforms a relation or another routine; a relation specifies what a rationale establishes. Their mutual application continues when the operands are the definitions of the language or its interpreters. The point is not that three kinds of artifact coexist, but that an established relationship participates in subsequent computation with its actual dependencies intact." nil)
